  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 444 AM CDT Fri Jun 26 2026\n\nHeat is the main story and the only story today. Zonal flow across\nthe CONUS with broad west-east ridge over the Gulf Coast today\nwill break down into the weekend and early next week. Amplifying\npattern will see ridge strengthen and become centered over the\nMississippi River Valley through early next week. 500mb heights\neventually peak at around 597dam over the Ohio River Valley mid\nweek. The combination of heat beneath this ridge and Gulf Coast\nhumidity will push heat index values to near 105 degrees in some\nplaces again today, but increasingly over 105 degrees tomorrow and\nSunday. Heat Advisories may be needed for the area in this time\nframe. And then Monday and Tuesday should see those values climb\nabove 110 degrees, with an Excessive Heat Warning possibly needed\nfor portions of the forecast area. As the core of the ridge shifts\nnorthward, easterly flow and returning tropical moisture will\nbring rain chances back to at least southern portions of the\nforecast area. Expect it to remain hot and humid with summery\nthunderstorms heading into early July. /NF/",
